::ENG3_U05_L03_GP_Q01::[MLA.ENG3.V.03] Sentence: The committee called the proposal "reckless" because it ignored every warning from the engineers. What is the connotative effect of the word "reckless"? {
~A. It suggests the proposal is simply new.#Not quite. "New" is neutral, but "reckless" carries a negative judgment about poor caution.
=B. It suggests the proposal is dangerously careless.#Correct. "Reckless" means careless in a way that may cause harm, so the connotation is negative. Notice how the answer uses the exact wording, evidence, or concept required by the standard.
~C. It suggests the proposal is carefully planned.#No. A carefully planned proposal would not be described as "reckless." Recheck the passage, context, or task wording and choose the option that preserves meaning and matches the standard.
~D. It suggests the proposal is impossible to understand.#No. "Reckless" comments on judgment and risk, not clarity. Recheck the passage, context, or task wording and choose the option that preserves meaning and matches the standard.
}

